  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mg</mi></math> and charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> is lying at the mid-point of two stationary particles kept at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;when each is carrying same charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>. If the free charged particle is displaced from its equilibrium position through distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. The particle executes SHM. Its angular frequency of oscillation will be _______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;(if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
